# Root .gitignore is SHARED across domains (ui/ + backend/). Keep every pattern
# domain-aware: anchor anything that targets one domain's build or runtime
# output (`/name/` for the repo root, `domain/**/name/` for a subtree) so it can
# never silently match another domain's source. Per-domain ignores (dist,
# .turbo, ...) live in that domain's own .gitignore. See CONTRIBUTING.md.

# Universal
node_modules
coverage
.scannerwork
.idea
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.swo
npm-debug.log

# Editor / agent scratch
.cursor/plans/
.cursor/rules/

# Generated config: each domain commits *.json.example and the real *.json is
# generated and ignored. Deliberate shared convention across ui/ and backend/.
!config/*.json.example
config/*.json

# Backend + repo-root runtime output. ANCHORED: the bare `status` / `store` /
# `tmp` patterns previously matched UI source dirs of the same name and swallowed
# them. MDK runtime root is repo-root/tmp (MDK_ROOT).
/tmp/
/status/
/store/
backend/**/tmp/
backend/**/status/
backend/**/store/

# Turborepo cache can materialize at the repo root when a ui/ task is run from
# here. ANCHORED so it never matches a domain's own .turbo (those stay ignored
# by each domain's .gitignore per the header note above).
/.turbo/

# WIP work. `/Checklist*` is anchored to the repo root so it cannot match UI
# component files (e.g. ui/.../ChecklistCard.tsx).
/Checklist*

# local / machine-specific
docs/scripts/check_bullet_stops.py
docs/reference/maintainers/notes.md

# Hand-authored skills live in /skills/ (repo root), symlinked into each
# client's expected directory (.claude/skills, .cursor/skills, ...) so every
# agent discovers the same files with zero duplication. The mdk-skill product
# suite is generated FROM packages/mdk-skill INTO those same client dirs via
# `npm run install:skills`, which resolves through the symlinks into /skills/.
# Every generated skill is named mdk*, so one glob ignores them all (a hand-kept
# list drifts as skills are added or renamed); the hand-authored mdk* skills are
# re-included below so a local run never gets committed alongside them.
/skills/mdk*/
!/skills/mdk-docs-style/
!/skills/mdk-skill-suite/

# Vale style rules. The rules live in tetherto/docs-template (the `vale` branch),
# checked out beside this repo at `.tether-vale-source` by CI and locally (see
# `.vale.ini`). It is an external checkout, never committed here: the public
# mirror must not ship the internal style source.
/.tether-vale-source

# Contributor email remapping. Kept out of the repo: the entries must contain
# real personal/corporate addresses to work, and the public mirror ships without
# git history, so shipping them would leak addresses the mirror otherwise lacks.
# Keep a local copy here if you want masked `git log` output.
.mailmap

# Vale style source (local tooling, not shipped)
.tether-vale-source
